{"name":"Anavar / oxandrolone voice risk","deep":true,"image":null,"mentions":32,"casual":{"lead":["Oxandrolone, known as Anavar, is an oral anabolic steroid once used medically for weight recovery and used by some for muscle and physique goals, including by women. This entry covers the voice effect: deepening is among its documented virilizing effects in women.","It is an androgen receptor agonist described as strongly anabolic with weak androgenic action, which is why women often choose it. Virilization still occurs, and its article states that such masculinizing changes, including voice deepening, can be irreversible. Voice change here is an off-target effect, not a studied goal."],"sections":[{"h":"How people use it","paras":["Women using it for physique purposes have often chosen it because it is described as more anabolic than androgenic. Non-medical use falls outside prescribing, and the voice effect is generally regarded as a risk rather than a goal."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Risks & side effects","paras":["Documented risks include voice deepening, hirsutism, menstrual changes, clitoral enlargement, liver damage, lipid changes, drug interactions and pregnancy contraindication. FDA approval was withdrawn in 2023, and it is a controlled substance."],"subs":[]}]},"gallery":[],"links":{"studies":[{"title":"Evaluating perceptions, comprehension, and awareness of anabolic androgenic steroid use among gym users in the Riyadh region of Saudi Arabia.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/42965187/","source":"Journal of family medicine and primary care","year":2026,"cites":null,"kind":null},{"title":"Oxandrolone Efficacy in Wound Healing in Burned and Decubitus Ulcer Patients: A Systematic Review.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/36127967/","source":"Cureus","year":2022,"cites":null,"kind":"Review"},{"title":"Delayed rhabdomyolysis secondary to anabolic-androgenic steroid use.","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/33199332/","source":"Clinical medicine (London, En